    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65384,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 396,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See the individual tumour types in the WHO classification of skin tumours [[Elder DE, Massi D, Scolyer RA, et al., editors. WHO classification of skin tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2018. (WHO classification of tumours series, 4th ed.; vol. 11). https://publications.iarc.fr/560.]].</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:32:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65385,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 396,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vulvar carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:32:02"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65386,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 396,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumour recurrence is common and some patients develop distant metastasis {20606537; 27832810; 12581149}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-09T16:32:02"
      }
    ],
